# What: Editor Files Block. Why: Editor and operating system settings belong to each machine, not the project. How: This ignores their folders and files, plus the Zone.Identifier markers Windows attaches to downloaded files.
*.njsproj
*.ntvs*
*.sln
*.suo
*.sw?
*:Zone.Identifier
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode/*



# What: Log Files Block. Why: Logs are local run output, not source. How: This ignores every log file and folder the package managers write.
*.log
lerna-debug.log*
logs
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*



# What: Generated And Local Files Block. Why: Build output, dependencies, local secrets, and test reports are recreated or kept per machine. How: This ignores the build output, node_modules, local env files, and the test suites' reports and run output.
*.env
*.local
dist
dist-ssr
node_modules
tests/output



# What: Re-Include Block. Why: A shared file inside an ignored folder still belongs in the project, and a re-include only works after the pattern it overrides. How: This re-includes .vscode/extensions.json, so the editor's extension recommendations stay shared.
!.vscode/extensions.json
